      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Mandatory Interstate RTO Paperwork &amp; Legal Formalities for Car Transportation In Chennai</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>When you plan to move a car across state borders in India, the paperwork can be as critical as the logistics itself. The most important documents you must have on hand are the Form 28 (No Objection Certificate), a copy of the original RC, a valid insurance policy and a recent PUC (Pollution Under Control) certification.</p>
<p>These items prove ownership, insurance coverage and environmental compliance, and they are mandatory for every auto transport company handling interstate vehicle transport.</p>

<p>Form 28 is issued by the Regional Transport Office (RTO) and confirms that the vehicle is not under any legal dispute or loan. The original RC copy establishes the vehicle’s identity, while the insurance policy protects against loss or damage during transit.</p>
<p>A PUC certification, valid for the last 30 days, is required by the Ministry of Environment and is checked by the transport crew before the vehicle leaves the state.</p>

